module

public import Mathlib.Data.Fin.Tuple.Take
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Ideal
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.RegularSequence
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.KoszulResolution
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Koszul.Regular
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The variables of a polynomial ring are a regular sequence

Let `R` be a nontrivial commutative ring. The variables `T₀, …, Tₙ` of `R[T₀, …, Tₙ]` form a
regular sequence, hence a Koszul-regular one ([Stacks, Tag 062F]), and therefore the extended
alternating Čech complex of `T₀, …, Tₙ` with coefficients in `R[T₀, …, Tₙ]` has cohomology
concentrated in the top degree `n + 1` ([Stacks, Tag 0G6L]).

That last statement is the algebraic content of the computation of the cohomology of the twists of
the structure sheaf on projective space ([Stacks, Tag 01XT]): the extended alternating Čech complex
of the variables is the Čech complex of the standard cover `ℙⁿ_R = ⋃ D₊(Tᵢ)` augmented by the
global sections, so its cohomology vanishing off degree `n + 1` is what forces
`H^q(ℙⁿ_R, 𝒪(d))` to vanish for `0 < q < n` and to be the degree-`d` part of `R[T₀, …, Tₙ]` for
`q = 0`.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.mem_span_X_image_of_X_mul_mem`: **the regularity criterion, in monomial form.** If
  `Tᵢ · f` lies in the ideal generated by a set of variables not containing `Tᵢ`, so does `f`.
* `MvPolynomial.one_notMem_span_X_image`: `1` is not in the ideal generated by any set of
  variables.
* `MvPolynomial.isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_X` and `MvPolynomial.isRegular_ofFn_X`: **the variables form
  a regular sequence.**
* `MvPolynomial.isKoszulRegular_X`: hence a Koszul-regular one, by [Stacks, Tag 062F].
* `MvPolynomial.cechComplex_homology_X_isZero`: **the extended alternating Čech complex of the
  variables has cohomology only in degree `n + 1`**, by [Stacks, Tag 0G6L].

## Implementation notes

**The whole proof is the monomial description of the ideal of a set of variables**,
`MvPolynomial.mem_ideal_span_X_image`: a polynomial lies in `(Tⱼ : j ∈ s)` exactly when every
monomial of its support has a positive exponent at some `j ∈ s`. Multiplying by `Tᵢ` translates
the support by `Finsupp.single i 1`, which changes no exponent away from `i`, so for `i ∉ s` the
criterion is unaffected and `Tᵢ` is a nonzerodivisor modulo `(Tⱼ : j ∈ s)`. No quotient of a
polynomial ring is identified with a smaller polynomial ring, and no induction on the number of
variables is performed; the usual argument through
`MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R ⧸ (T₀) ≅ MvPolynomial (Fin n) R` would need that identification,
which this repository and Mathlib both lack.

**The predecessor ideal is read off directly.** `RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular` asks for
regularity of the `i`-th element modulo the ideal of the first `i`, written
`Ideal.ofList (rs.take i)`; `MvPolynomial.ofList_take_ofFn_X` identifies that with
`Ideal.span (X '' {j | (j : ℕ) < i})` through `Fin.ofFn_take_eq_take_ofFn`, so the monomial
criterion applies verbatim. `MvPolynomial.ideal_smul_top` turns the submodule `I • ⊤` of the ring
back into the ideal `I`.

**Nontriviality of `R` is needed only for the last condition of regularity**, that the quotient by
the sequence is nonzero: over the zero ring every ideal is the unit ideal. Weak regularity holds
with no hypothesis on `R`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 062F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G6L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G6L)

## What is not done

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. Tag 062F sits on
`Koszul.isKoszulRegularOn_and_isKoszulRegular_of_regular` and Tag 0G6L on
`Cech.cechComplex_homology_isZero_of_isKoszulRegular`; what is here is the instance of those two
at the variables of a polynomial ring, which is an input to [Stacks, Tag 01XT] and not an
assertion of any tag.

Tag 01XT itself is **not** proved. What remains between
`MvPolynomial.cechComplex_homology_X_isZero` and it is the comparison of the degree-`d` graded
piece of `Cech.cechComplex X R[T]` with the Čech complex of the standard cover of `ℙⁿ_R` for
`𝒪(d)`: the terms correspond by [Stacks, Tag 01M6]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.associatedModuleSheafStandardOpenEquiv`, whose
compatibility with restriction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.standardOpenEquiv_restrict`), and the graded piece is a
split subcomplex, so its cohomology is a direct summand of the cohomology computed here; the
passage from Čech to derived cohomology is [Stacks, Tag 01XD] together with [Stacks, Tag 01FJ] and
[Stacks, Tag 01FM], all three in the library.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

namespace MvPolynomial

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {σ : Type v}

/-! ### The monomial criterion -/

/-- **A variable outside a set of variables is a nonzerodivisor modulo their ideal.** If `Tᵢ · f`
lies in the ideal generated by the variables indexed by `s` and `i ∉ s`, then `f` lies in that
ideal.

Multiplication by `Tᵢ` translates the support by `Finsupp.single i 1`, which leaves every exponent
away from `i` unchanged, so `MvPolynomial.mem_ideal_span_X_image` transfers across it. -/
theorem mem_span_X_image_of_X_mul_mem {s : Set σ} {i : σ} (hi : i ∉ s)
    {f : MvPolynomial σ R} (h : X i * f ∈ Ideal.span (X '' s : Set (MvPolynomial σ R))) :
    f ∈ Ideal.span (X '' s : Set (MvPolynomial σ R)) := by
  rw [mem_ideal_span_X_image] at h ⊢
  intro m hm
  have hm' : Finsupp.single i 1 + m ∈ (X i * f).support := by
    rw [support_X_mul]
    exact Finset.mem_map.mpr ⟨m, hm, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨j, hjs, hj⟩ := h _ hm'
  refine ⟨j, hjs, ?_⟩
  have hij : i ≠ j := fun hji => hi (hji ▸ hjs)
  simpa [Finsupp.single_apply, hij] using hj

/-- **The ideal generated by a set of variables is proper**: the monomial of `1` has no positive
exponent. -/
theorem one_notMem_span_X_image [Nontrivial R] {s : Set σ} :
    (1 : MvPolynomial σ R) ∉ Ideal.span (X '' s : Set (MvPolynomial σ R)) := by
  rw [mem_ideal_span_X_image]
  intro h
  obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := h 0 (by simp)
  exact hj rfl

/-- For an ideal of a commutative ring, the submodule `I • ⊤` of the ring is `I` itself. This is
the shape `RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular` states its predecessor ideal in. -/
theorem ideal_smul_top (S : Type u) [CommRing S] (I : Ideal S) :
    I • (⊤ : Submodule S S) = I := by
  refine le_antisymm (Submodule.smul_le.2 fun r hr x _ => I.mul_mem_right _ hr) fun x hx => ?_
  simpa using Submodule.smul_mem_smul hx (Submodule.mem_top (R := S) (x := (1 : S)))

/-! ### The variables as a regular sequence -/

/-- The ideal of the first `m` variables, as `RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular` presents it. -/
theorem ofList_take_ofFn_X (n m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ n + 1) :
    Ideal.ofList ((List.ofFn (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)).take m)
      = Ideal.span (X '' {j : Fin (n+1) | (j : ℕ) < m}) := by
  rw [← Fin.ofFn_take_eq_take_ofFn hm]
  have hset : {r : MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R | r ∈ List.ofFn (Fin.take m hm X)}
      = X '' {j : Fin (n+1) | (j : ℕ) < m} := by
    refine Set.ext fun r => ?_
    constructor
    · intro hr
      obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := List.mem_ofFn.mp hr
      exact ⟨Fin.castLE hm j, by simp, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩
      exact List.mem_ofFn.mpr ⟨⟨j, hj⟩, by simp [Fin.take, Fin.castLE]⟩
  exact congrArg Ideal.span hset

/-- **The variables of a polynomial ring form a weakly regular sequence**, with no hypothesis on
the coefficient ring. -/
@[sga "6 VII 1.2" "partial"]
theorem isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_X (n : ℕ) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular (MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)
      (List.ofFn (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)) := by
  rw [RingTheory.Sequence.isWeaklyRegular_iff]
  intro i hi
  have hin : i < n + 1 := by simpa using hi
  rw [ideal_smul_top, ofList_take_ofFn_X (R := R) n i hin.le,
    isSMulRegular_iff_right_eq_zero_of_smul]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨f, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
  rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, List.getElem_ofFn,
    smul_eq_mul] at hx
  exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).2 (mem_span_X_image_of_X_mul_mem (by simp) hx)

/-- **The variables of a polynomial ring over a nontrivial ring form a regular sequence.**
Nontriviality enters only through the properness of the ideal they generate. -/
@[sga "6 VII 1.2" "(T_1, special case"]
theorem isRegular_ofFn_X [Nontrivial R] (n : ℕ) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)
      (List.ofFn (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)) where
  toIsWeaklyRegular := isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_X n
  top_ne_smul := by
    rw [ideal_smul_top, show (List.ofFn (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R))
        = (List.ofFn (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)).take (n+1) by simp,
      ofList_take_ofFn_X (R := R) n (n+1) le_rfl]
    exact ((Ideal.ne_top_iff_one _).2 one_notMem_span_X_image).symm

/-- **The variables of a polynomial ring are a Koszul-regular sequence**, by [Stacks, Tag 062F]. -/
@[sga "6 VII 1.2" "more general"]
theorem isKoszulRegular_X [Nontrivial R] (n : ℕ) :
    Koszul.IsKoszulRegular (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R) :=
  (Koszul.isKoszulRegularOn_and_isKoszulRegular_of_regular
    (M := MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)).2.2 (isRegular_ofFn_X n)

/-- **The extended alternating Čech complex of the variables has cohomology only in the top
degree.** This is [Stacks, Tag 0G6L] at the Koszul-regular sequence `T₀, …, Tₙ`, and it is the
algebraic content of the cohomology of the twists of the structure sheaf on `ℙⁿ_R`
([Stacks, Tag 01XT]): the complex is the Čech complex of the standard cover of `ℙⁿ_R`, augmented
by the global sections. -/
theorem cechComplex_homology_X_isZero [Nontrivial R] (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ) (hp : p ≠ n + 1) :
    CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero
      ((Cech.cechComplex (X : Fin (n+1) → MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)
        (MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) R)).homology p) :=
  Cech.cechComplex_homology_isZero_of_isKoszulRegular _ (isKoszulRegular_X n) p hp

end MvPolynomial

end
